Also use the imported Customer class to tidy the fully-qualified names? The original used `com.example.demo.entity.Customer` fully qualified. I'll import it for readability — behavior identical. Actually, minimal churn is a virtue; but importing is cleaner. I'll import `com.example.demo.entity.Customer` and use the simple name. Both tests keep the same assertions.

Strictness note: MockitoExtension defaults to STRICT_STUBS. In `byEmailDelegatesToRepository`, stub `repository.findByEmail("x@example.com")` → used by `service.byEmail("x@example.com")` ✓. In `allReturnsRepositoryList`, stub `findAll()` → used ✓. No unused stubs → no UnnecessaryStubbingException.

